# {{ package_name }}

A **cohort adapter** for building-energy-analysis (BEA): it turns one data source into the cohort
`{{ class_name }}`, which BEA finds by name through its `bea.cohorts` entry point. Written against
BEA's **cohort contract {{ contract_version }}**, rendered from `c-energie/bea-cohort-template`.

## Commands

Run from the repository root:

```bash
pip install -e .
TEST_TIER=fast python -m unittest discover
```

Reinstall after editing `pyproject.toml`: an entry point is read from installed metadata. The
first run generates `tests/Configuration_files/` (gitignored), with every test class `on`.

## Vocabulary

Use BEA's words ([CONTEXT.md](https://github.com/c-energie/building-energy-analysis/blob/master/CONTEXT.md)).
A data source is never a "dataset": in BEA a **Dataset** is the data of one household. This
package makes a **cohort** of **households**, each identified by a **PUPRN**. Class names stay
`…Cohort` and `…Dataset` even when the package name says `-dataset`.

## Layout

- `src/{{ import_name }}/settings.py`: the source schema, `[units]`, sensor uncertainties
- `src/{{ import_name }}/cohort.py`: `{{ class_name }}`, reads the source
- `src/{{ import_name }}/household.py`: `{{ household_class_name }}`, one household
- `src/{{ import_name }}/variables.py`: a `Variable` per quantity a model reads
- `src/{{ import_name }}/toy_data/`: the toy, the tests' fixture
- `tests/__init__.py`: BEA's `CohortContractTests`, and the toy end to end

## Rules

- **Never commit data**, and never read a data file's values to learn its layout. To describe a
  source, run BEA's `skills/bea-cohort-adapter/scripts/inspect_source.py`: a schema-only report.
- Real paths go in the machine layer's `[input_dirs] data_dir`, never in this package.
- Never weaken a contract test, and never edit BEA to make one pass.
- Leave `contract_version` as rendered. A contract bump is `copier update`, from a clean tree.

